<title>GREECE: SCHEDULE ON GREEK CORPORATE BRIEFING.</title>
<headline>SCHEDULE ON GREEK CORPORATE BRIEFING.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corporate briefing of Greek institutional investors continue with St George Mills , the flour mill, and Sportsman , the casual clothing and sportswear retailer on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The presentations are part of a scheme of briefings over the fundamentals and business plans of listed Greek companies which are held on a weekly basis in Athens at Greece's Association of Institutional Investors.</p>
<p>A total of 37 Greek listed companies has come under the scrutiny of Greek institutional investors since Dec 18, 1996.</p>
<p>Around 30 more companies are slated for a presentation in the coming months, an Association official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The schedule for the coming weeks is as follows:</p>
<p>Apr 23, 1997   St George Mills SA </p>
<p>		   Sportsman SA </p>
<p>May 7, 1997    Yalco SA </p>
<p>		   Mytilineos SA </p>
<p>		   General Commerce SA </p>
<p>14, 1997	 Viohalko SA </p>
<p>		   Hellenic Cables SA </p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301-3311812-4</p>
</text>
